{"number":1,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-A1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"In OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs REPLACE the closed union MaterialCategory (MaterialLibrary.fs:67) with DATA. Add CategoryId (a Guid-backed single-case DU with a .value accessor and a static create : unit -> CategoryId minting Guid.NewGuid, mirroring MaterialId at MaterialLibrary.fs:27); CategoryVisibility = SelectableOnCreate | HiddenOnCreate and CategoryOrigin = BuiltInCategory | UserCategory (named two-case DUs, never a bool); and the record MaterialCategory = { id : CategoryId; name : string; visibility : CategoryVisibility; origin : CategoryOrigin }. Add a CategoryIds module of FIXED literal Guids (mirroring MaterialLibrary.MaterialIds at :51) and a seeded standardCategories : MaterialCategory list with Glass/Metal/Semiconductor/Crystal as BuiltInCategory/SelectableOnCreate and Vacuum as BuiltInCategory/HiddenOnCreate. Re-type MaterialEntry.category (:119) and MaterialQuery.category (:368) to CategoryId / CategoryId option, re-seed every builtInEntries category (:252 onward) to the matching CategoryIds value, and re-express byCategory (:146) and byQuery (:415) as CategoryId filters. Re-point the consumers to read the seeded catalogue: MaterialEditorView.categoryRow and its hardcoded list (MaterialEditorView.fs:551,561) plus the model category field / ChooseCategory (:177,188) offer only SelectableOnCreate categories from standardCategories (Vacuum removed, not greyed); TableAndElementRotationView.materialCategories / materialCategoryCode / materialCategoryLabel / materialCategoryOfCode (TableAndElementRotationView.fs:1910-1935), the facet (:2002), and the entry.category display (:2159) resolve the name through the catalogue by CategoryId. No closed-union path remains.","acceptance":"After the change, no domain record or signature carries the closed MaterialCategory union (MaterialEntry.category and MaterialQuery.category are CategoryId-typed), a category name resolves through the seeded catalogue by id, and the create picker offers every SelectableOnCreate category and no HiddenOnCreate one, with the solution building and OpticalConstructor.Tests green.","section":"Part A - Categories: open, editable, Guid-keyed (CRITICAL - land first)"}
{"number":2,"anchor":"ADD_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-A2","id":"STORE_XDUO_0003","name":"CategoryProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Domain","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[1],"how_to":"In OpticalConstructor.Domain, beside the step-1 category catalogue, declare the mutating category write-seam following the LibraryProxy / MaterialProxy functional-proxy convention (ElementId.fs:276; MaterialLibrary.fs:389). Add CategoryError with UnknownCategoryId, DuplicateCategoryId, CategoryStillReferenced, BuiltInNotRemovable and InvalidCategory, each carrying reason : string; and the [<ReferenceEquality>] record CategoryProxy with listCategories : unit -> Result<MaterialCategory list, CategoryError>, addCategory : MaterialCategory -> Result<unit, CategoryError>, updateCategory : MaterialCategory -> Result<unit, CategoryError>, removeCategory : CategoryId -> Result<unit, CategoryError>. Add a validateCategory helper rejecting a blank name as InvalidCategory (the validateEntry precedent, MaterialLibrary.fs:430). Provide a mock (an inline stub record over a fixed category list) plus a mock-driven test in OpticalConstructor.Tests exercising every field through its exact signature.","acceptance":"After the step, a mock-driven test MUST build a stub CategoryProxy and exercise all four functions through their exact signatures, and it passes."}
{"number":3,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-A2","id":"STORE_XDUO_0003","name":"CategoryProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[2],"how_to":"Implement CategoryProxy.createInMemory taking materialsReferencingCategory : CategoryId -> MaterialEntry list and closing over a ref Map<CategoryId, MaterialCategory> seeded from standardCategories - the elevated CategoryId is the Map key directly (the SampleProxy / MaterialProxy.createInMemory precedent, ElementId.fs:616,686). addCategory validates the name then hard-blocks a duplicate id (DuplicateCategoryId); updateCategory validates then replaces a known id and rejects an unknown one (UnknownCategoryId) - built-ins ARE renamable; removeCategory refuses a BuiltInCategory (BuiltInNotRemovable) and, for a UserCategory, returns CategoryStillReferenced naming the referencing materials whenever materialsReferencingCategory returns any (it never cascades, never silently deletes), else removes it. Add a module-level materialsReferencingCategory lookup over a MaterialProxy.listMaterials result (the samplesReferencing precedent, ElementId.fs:740) filtering entries whose category equals the id. Mutation stays inside the closure (the IO boundary). Unit tests in OpticalConstructor.Tests: add/rename/remove round-trips with fixed Guids, the referenced-category hard block, the built-in-not-removable block, and the duplicate-add rejection.","acceptance":"After createInMemory lands, removeCategory on a category referenced by a seeded material MUST return Error CategoryStillReferenced and removeCategory on a built-in MUST return Error BuiltInNotRemovable, both leaving the store unchanged, while add/rename/remove of an unreferenced user category round-trip deterministically with fixed Guids."}
{"number":4,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-A3","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[2],"how_to":"Add a pure, Avalonia-free Domain edit model CategoryEditor (a new OpticalConstructor.Domain module) mirroring the message-DU discipline of MaterialComplexityEditor (state + one message DU + a Result-returning apply): a state record over the current MaterialCategory list plus any in-progress inline edit, and messages BeginAddCategory (mints CategoryId.create () as a UserCategory / SelectableOnCreate row with a blank name), SetCategoryName of CategoryId * string, and RemoveCategoryRow of CategoryId, plus a commit projection producing the add / rename / remove intents the host dispatches to CategoryProxy. Rejections (blank name) reuse the typed CategoryError from step 2. Every message arm is unit-tested without a window in OpticalConstructor.Tests.","acceptance":"After the step, applying BeginAddCategory then SetCategoryName over the CategoryEditor state MUST yield a UserCategory / SelectableOnCreate row carrying the typed name, and a blank name MUST surface the typed InvalidCategory, verified by pure unit tests."}
{"number":5,"anchor":"ADD_COMPONENT","ac":"AC-A4","id":"UICOMP_XDUO_0005","name":"CategoryControls","kind":"component","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Controls","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[4],"how_to":"Create OpticalConstructor.Controls/CategoryControls.fs copying the domain-free LibraryControls shape (pure Row and State records, a Handlers record of unit-returning functions, one [<RequireQualifiedAccess>] module UiIds of [<Literal>] intent-named ids): a category list with an inline name box per row and Add / Rename(save) / Remove verbs, a built-in row whose name is editable but whose Remove is omitted (removed, not greyed), and an inline block-message slot for CategoryStillReferenced / BuiltInNotRemovable. Stable intent-named ids: CategoriesList, AddCategoryButton, CategoryNameBox, RemoveCategoryButton, CategorySaveButton, CategoryCancelButton, CategoryBlockMessage. The control renders the rows it is given and never touches a proxy (the host flattens). Headless structure test in OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests: mount the view over a known State, assert every UiIds control exists, and assert a simulated Add click invokes the add handler.","acceptance":"After the step, the headless test MUST mount CategoryControls over a known State, find every UiIds control, and observe that a simulated Add click invokes the add handler."}
{"number":6,"anchor":"ADD_COMPONENT","ac":"AC-A5","id":"UICOMP_XDUO_0006","name":"CategoryEditorWindow","kind":"component","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","touches":["OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[3,4,5],"how_to":"Create the Category editor window in OpticalConstructor.TestWindows beside the existing MaterialEditorWindow / SampleEditorWindow, over the step-4 CategoryEditor edit model and the step-5 CategoryControls. Add opens an inline UserCategory / SelectableOnCreate row; Rename edits name inline (built-ins renamable); Remove is confirm-gated inline and surfaces CategoryStillReferenced (naming the referencing materials) or BuiltInNotRemovable; Save calls the matching CategoryProxy verb (addCategory / updateCategory / removeCategory), Cancel discards; Save/Cancel sit in one row with distinct positive/negative styling. Stable UiIds reuse the step-5 constants plus CategoryEditorWindow. Headless tests in OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests drive the window by UiIds over a stub CategoryProxy: add-then-list grows the list, rename updates the name, and removing a referenced category surfaces the block and leaves the list unchanged.","acceptance":"After the step, headless tests MUST drive CategoryEditorWindow by UiIds over a stub CategoryProxy: Add grows the list, Rename updates a name, and removing a referenced or built-in category surfaces the typed block and leaves the list unchanged."}
{"number":7,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-B1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"In OpticalConstructor.Controls/Ribbon.fs make Ribbon.view (Ribbon.fs:90) host only the ACTIVE bay's content in ONE stable, keyed content slot instead of rendering every bay's pane with IsVisible toggles (Ribbon.fs:95-103). Key the single content ContentControl/Border by the active bay name (SubPatchOptions.OnChangeOf the active name) so FuncUI patches a pane only against its own previous self and never recycles a styled, named control across two DIFFERENT bays - the hazard the Ribbon.fs:84-89 comment documents. The activeBay selection (Ribbon.fs:79) and the tab strip are unchanged; UiIds.pane (Ribbon.fs:44) now names the single active slot. Headless test in OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests: selecting each bay in turn shows exactly that bay's content and no other pane is realized.","acceptance":"After the change, the ribbon MUST realize only the selected bay's content in one keyed slot, selecting each bay shows exactly its content, and no styled-element recycling error occurs, verified by the headless UI tests.","section":"Part B - Ribbon hosting: single active pane, full-surface bays, ordering"}
{"number":8,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-B2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[7],"how_to":"Add a bay content-mode two-case DU (never a bool) - a table bay (the canvas plus its pan/zoom/rotate gestures) vs a full-surface bay (its own IView replaces the canvas area) - carried on Ribbon.Bay (Ribbon.fs:25) or mapped by the Main host from bay name to mode. In TableAndElementRotationView.mainView (TableAndElementRotationView.fs:2281) render the table canvas and its pointer/wheel handlers ONLY for a table bay; a full-surface bay fills the whole area below the ribbon strip with the bay's content and wires no table gestures. Mark the Materials and Library bays full-surface (materialsBay / samplesBay in mainBays, TableAndElementRotationView.fs:2265) and, now that step-7 pane hosting is order-independent, move Materials and Library to be the LAST two bays in mainBays and BayNames.all (TableAndElementRotationView.fs:239), retiring the Details-LAST pin and the deferred-reorder comment (TableAndElementRotationView.fs:235-238). Headless MainWorkbench ui-smoke tests drive the reordered, full-surface bays green.","acceptance":"After the change, the ribbon MUST show Materials and Library as the last two bays, each occupying the full surface below the ribbon with no table canvas, while a table bay keeps its canvas and gestures, verified by the headless MainWorkbench tests."}
{"number":9,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-A6","touches":["OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[3,6,8],"how_to":"Host-wire the category catalogue into TableAndElementRotationView. Thread the step-3 CategoryProxy into the host model through initMainWith (TableAndElementRotationView.fs:319) beside the material/sample proxies, updating the DefaultStores composition (TableAndElementRotationView.fs:256) and the OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs composition call mechanically so the solution builds (the step-19 WIRE_UI owns the composition acceptance). Add a Categories... verb to the Materials bay that opens the step-6 CategoryEditorWindow via the EditorLaunchers seam (TableAndElementRotationView.fs:117). Drive the material-editor create picker and the Materials-bay category facet from CategoryProxy.listCategories: the create picker excludes HiddenOnCreate; the facet lists the catalogue with option code = CategoryId Guid string and label = name. After every category add/rename/remove the bay re-queries the proxy so the picker and facet refresh in the same render pass. Headless tests in OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests: the Categories... verb opens the editor, and a category renamed through the proxy re-labels the create picker and facet.","acceptance":"After the step, headless tests MUST show the Materials bay Categories... verb opening the CategoryEditorWindow, and a category renamed through the proxy re-labelling the create picker and facet in the same render pass."}
{"number":10,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-C1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"In OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs extend the optically-active and magnetic rungs to a Constant vs Dispersive sub-branch (the eps ladder pattern). Generalise MaterialComplexityEditState (MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:102) to store, per symmetry-allowed gyration component (gyrationComponents, :385) and per Polder component, BOTH the constant value (the current GyrationClass<RhoValue> at :117 / PolderValue<MuValue> at :123) AND a dispersive DispersionModel edited through the SAME DispersionModels.modelParameters + raw SumOfTerms surface built in 0033 (DispersionModels.fs:291), plus an activity and a magnetic Dispersive sub-toggle; unchecking Dispersive restores the constant losslessly (the module's existing lossless discipline). toComplexity (:699) builds RhoWithDispValue / MuWithDispValue from each component's DispersionFormula when the sub-toggle is on, RhoWithoutDispValue / MuWithoutDispValue otherwise. ofComplexity (:749) seeds from a dispersive RhoWithDispValue / MuWithDispValue and the UnsupportedComplexity case (:140,784,790) is DELETED (no view-only fallback, section 0.2). The engine toRhoWithDisp (OpticalProperties/Active.fs:152) and toMuWithDisp (Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs:644) are UNCHANGED. Unit tests in OpticalConstructor.Tests: toComplexity of an on-Dispersive gyration and Polder builds the WithDisp value whose per-wavelength assembly equals the engine toRhoWithDisp / toMuWithDisp, and ofComplexity then toComplexity round-trips a dispersive rho and mu by sampled tensor value.","acceptance":"After the step, a dispersive gyration and a dispersive Polder permeability MUST derive through toComplexity into RhoWithDispValue / MuWithDispValue whose per-wavelength assembly equals the engine builders, seed back through ofComplexity value-identically by sampled tensor, and the UnsupportedComplexity view-only case MUST no longer exist.","section":"Part C - Dispersive gyration rho and Polder mu editing"}
{"number":11,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-C2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[10],"how_to":"In OpticalConstructor.TestWindows/MaterialEditorView.fs surface the step-10 Constant/Dispersive sub-branch on the optically-active and magnetic rungs: a per-rung Dispersive sub-toggle that, when on, replaces each symmetry-allowed gyration component box and each Polder component box with a DispersionModel coefficient editor (the existing per-axis modelParameters / SumOfTerms box surface). Add stable intent-named UiIds for the two sub-toggles and the per-component formula editors. Headless tests in OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests drive the window by UiIds: enabling the activity Dispersive sub-toggle exposes a formula box per symmetry-allowed gyration component, enabling the magnetic Dispersive sub-toggle exposes the Polder component formula boxes, and unchecking each restores the constant boxes.","acceptance":"After the step, headless tests MUST show the activity and magnetic Dispersive sub-toggles exposing a per-component dispersion-formula editor for each symmetry-allowed component, and unchecking each sub-toggle restoring the constant component boxes."}
{"number":12,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-D1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"In OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs extend validateSample (ElementId.fs:596), which today checks the name only, with a structure-content rule: a Sample whose structure has no films AND no substrate (films = [] and substrate = None on SampleStructure, ElementId.fs:103) is structurally empty and returns Error (InvalidSample reason). Both addSample and updateSample already run validateSample (ElementId.fs:641,651), so the guard applies on every save. Update the OpticalConstructor.Tests that save a structurally-empty sample to add stack content (they were pinning the name-only contract this decision supersedes), and add a test asserting a name-carrying but structurally-empty sample is rejected as InvalidSample.","acceptance":"After the step, addSample and updateSample MUST reject a sample with no films and no substrate as Error (InvalidSample _) even when its name is non-blank, and the previously name-only empty-sample tests are updated to carry stack content and pass.","section":"Part D - Sample-editor polish"}
{"number":13,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-D2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[1],"how_to":"In OpticalConstructor.TestWindows/SampleEditorView.fs make the material picker in materialRow (SampleEditorView.fs:647) searchable: add a search box and a catalogue-driven category facet (the step-1 seeded categories, mirroring the Materials bay facet) that filter the resolved material list the window loads once from MaterialProxy.listMaterials (SampleEditorView.fs:6). The by-MaterialId selection contract (ChooseMaterial of MaterialId, SampleEditorView.fs:190) is unchanged. Add stable intent-named UiIds for the search box and the category facet. Headless tests in OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests: typing a fragment and selecting a category filter narrows the material options, and choosing a filtered option still dispatches ChooseMaterial with its MaterialId.","acceptance":"After the step, headless tests MUST show the sample-editor material picker filtering its options by a search fragment and by a category facet while still selecting a material by MaterialId."}
{"number":14,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-D3","touches":["OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"Give SmpMakeMultilayer a distinct launcher path (today SmpAdd and SmpMakeMultilayer both open a blank editor, TableAndElementRotationView.fs:428,855; the makeMultilayer handler is at :2065). Extend the Sample editor init with a new-with-seed SampleStructure path - distinct from the blank Add and from a Some existing update-in-place - that opens a NEW sample pre-seeded with a foldable starter period: one Repeated period group of a 2-layer cell (SampleStructure at ElementId.fs:103; PeriodGroup / Repeated at ElementId.fs:89,98) ready for the SampleStackEditor K-stepper (MakeRepeatBlock / SetRepeatCount, SampleStackEditor.fs:79). Save still mints a fresh SampleId (SampleId.create, ElementId.fs:45). Headless tests in OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests: SmpMakeMultilayer opens the editor showing the seeded 2-layer period, and Save persists a new sample through SampleProxy.addSample.","acceptance":"After the step, SmpMakeMultilayer MUST open a NEW sample seeded with a foldable 2-layer period (distinct from the blank Add), and Save MUST persist it through SampleProxy.addSample under a freshly minted SampleId, verified by headless tests."}
{"number":15,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-E1","touches":["Berreman","BerremanTests","OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"Make the transcendental dispersion models first-class in a dispersive segment. In Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs add a third EpsAxisDispersion case (Dispersion.fs:306) representing an evaluated-directly model: it carries a WaveLength -> ComplexRefractionIndex closure exactly as the engine's own EpsWithDisp case does in this file (Dispersion.fs:11-12), and its complexIndex returns that closure applied to w. Because a function-typed union case removes F# structural equality type-wide, mark EpsAxisDispersion [<CustomEquality; NoComparison>] with equality that compares RealNK / ComplexEps structurally and the evaluated case by closure reference, so DispersionModel, EpsWithDispValue and MaterialComplexity keep the equality the existing Assert.Equal(model, back) and Assert.Equal(Ok axis, toEpsAxis model) tests use (OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs:121,349). In OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs make toEpsAxis (DispersionModels.fs:605) lower the four transcendental models TaucLorentz / GaussianOscillator / ForouhiBloomer / BrendelBormann (currently Error NotAFiniteTermSum at :666-673) to the new evaluated case via DispersionModels.evaluate (:486); toEpsAxis becomes total (all ten models lower), so remove the now-unreachable EpsAxisLoweringError / NotAFiniteTermSum (:505) and simplify toEpsValue / toOpticalProperties (:700,716). In OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs drop lowerAxis's error mapping and the SegmentNotLowerable case (:132,634,637) so toComplexity (:699) builds a dispersive segment for a transcendental model, and add a modelParameters arm for the evaluated case returning no editable term scalars. Update the four tests that asserted Error NotAFiniteTermSum (DispersionModelsTests.fs:331,377,540) and the Assert.Equal(Ok axis, toEpsAxis model) shape (:349) to the total outcome. Tests in OpticalConstructor.Tests: for each of the four models the lowered EpsAxisDispersion.complexIndex equals DispersionModels.evaluate across a sampled wavelength grid within tolerance, and a MaterialComplexity carrying a transcendental dispersive segment derives and evaluates without SegmentNotLowerable.","acceptance":"After the step, toEpsAxis MUST lower all ten models (the four transcendental to the evaluated case), the four NotAFiniteTermSum errors and SegmentNotLowerable MUST no longer exist, and a transcendental dispersive segment's complexIndex MUST match DispersionModels.evaluate across a sampled grid within tolerance while building through toComplexity.","section":"Part E - Material-editor preview and transcendental models"}
{"number":16,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-E2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[15],"how_to":"Embed the shared dual-axis ScottPlot chart as the Material editor's live n/k preview and the Materials-bay View panel, replacing the primitive canvas. In OpticalConstructor.Controls expose an inline/embeddable form of the dual-axis ScottPlot chart control (an embeddable AvaPlot host reusing ExperimentChart / ChartStyle and the ChartWindow rebuild path, ChartWindow.fs:11-19, with the n-left / k-right axes) - not only the pop-out window. In OpticalConstructor.TestWindows/MaterialEditorView.fs embed that control as the live preview (MaterialEditorView.fs:856) and use it for the Materials-bay View panel, building the chart model through the unchanged NkDispersionChart.nkDispersionChart builder (NkDispersionChart.fs:55) and its nkDispersionStyle left/right assignment (:76); DELETE the primitive NkDispersionChart.inlineCanvas (NkDispersionChart.fs:108). Every model kind, including the four transcendental (step 15), draws n and k. The embedded control MUST render under the Avalonia.Headless ui-smoke frame without throwing so the gate stays green. Headless render tests in OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests: the Material editor preview and the Materials View panel render one frame carrying the embedded chart, for a dispersive (including transcendental) and a non-dispersive entry.","acceptance":"After the step, the Material editor preview and Materials View panel MUST embed the shared dual-axis ScottPlot chart (inlineCanvas deleted), draw n and k for every model kind including the four transcendental, and render under the headless ui-smoke frame without throwing."}
{"number":17,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-E3","touches":["OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"In OpticalConstructor.TestWindows/MaterialEditorView.fs present the primary eps branch as two mutually-exclusive options Constant / Dispersive instead of the sticky Dispersive toggle (togglesRow, MaterialEditorView.fs:594,604, 'off = constant n, k'). The two options map to the same SetDispersion (NonDispersive / DispersiveSegments) message so the derived model is unchanged (cosmetic). Update the absorbingToggle / dispersiveToggle acceptance tests (the ids at MaterialEditorView.fs:56,58) to the two-option model, and keep the Absorbing sub-option in the Constant branch only (removed, not greyed, under Dispersive).","acceptance":"After the step, the eps branch MUST present Constant and Dispersive as two mutually-exclusive options selecting NonDispersive / DispersiveSegments, with the updated toggle tests green and the derived model unchanged."}
{"number":18,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-F1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.App"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"Sweep the build warning-clean per section 0.6 across the touched projects: resolve any FS#### warning originating in the files this spec edits, and - if the build emits MSB3277 (conflicting assembly versions) from the WebView2 reference chain the Ui project carries (Microsoft.Web.WebView2, OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj:176, used by the ChartHosts adapters at :75,80) - resolve it at the reference level (constrain or drop the offending reference), never with a suppression. Only the exempt NuGet advisories (NU1701, NU1901-NU1904) may remain. Verify with dotnet build Berreman.slnx -c Release that no FS#### or MSB3277 warning from our code remains.","acceptance":"After the step, dotnet build Berreman.slnx -c Release MUST complete with no FS#### warning from our code and no MSB3277 assembly-version conflict, only the exempt NU1701 / NU1901-NU1904 third-party advisories remaining.","section":"Part F - Warning cleanup and composition root"}
{"number":19,"anchor":"WIRE_UI","ac":"AC-W1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[9,16],"how_to":"Finalize the composition root: in OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs build CategoryProxy.createInMemory (its materialsReferencingCategory lookup backed by the materials store) beside the existing SampleProxy / MaterialProxy / Library / Experiments proxies (Program.fs:138-140) and inject all of them through initMainWith; the launcher path is otherwise unchanged. Verify the whole surface headless: the ui-smoke suite renders one frame for the reordered full-surface Materials and Library bays, the Selector / Experiments / Details bays, and the Material / Sample / Category editor windows without throwing.","acceptance":"After composition, launching the Main window MUST wire the in-memory CategoryProxy at the root beside the material/sample proxies, and the ui-smoke suite MUST render the reordered full-surface Materials and Library bays and all three editor windows without throwing, with every test gate at or above its baseline count."}
